(window.STEP_DATA = window.STEP_DATA || {})[11] = {"n":11,"set":"B","level":"Intermediate","band":"B1 60% · B2 40%","sec":[{"id":"R","name":"Reading Comprehension","ar":"فهم المقروء","min":70,"from":1,"to":40,"g":[{"t":"The science of tides","p":["Anyone who has spent a day at the beach has probably noticed that the sea does not stay in the same place. Twice a day, in most coastal areas, the water slowly rises up the shore and then falls back again. These regular changes in sea level are called tides, and although they may look simple, they are the result of powerful forces acting across hundreds of thousands of kilometres of space.","The main cause of tides is the gravity of the Moon. Every object in the universe pulls on every other object, and the Moon's gravity pulls on the Earth and everything on it, including the oceans. Because water can move freely, the ocean on the side of the Earth facing the Moon is pulled slightly towards it, creating a bulge of water. At the same time, a second bulge forms on the opposite side of the Earth. This happens because the Moon pulls the solid Earth more strongly than it pulls the water on the far side, which is effectively 'left behind'.","As the Earth rotates once every twenty-four hours, each coastline passes through both bulges. When a place moves into a bulge, it experiences high tide; when it moves between them, it has low tide. However, the Moon is also moving in its orbit around the Earth, so the tides arrive about fifty minutes later each day. This is why the times of high and low tide change from day to day.","The Sun also affects tides, although its influence is less than half that of the Moon, because it is so much farther away. When the Sun, Moon and Earth are in a straight line, at new moon and full moon, their forces combine to produce especially high and especially low tides, known as spring tides. The name has nothing to do with the season; it comes from the idea of the water 'springing up'. When the Sun and Moon pull at right angles to each other, the difference between high and low tide is smaller. These are called neap tides.","The shape of the coast and the sea floor can make tides much larger or smaller. In enclosed seas, such as the Mediterranean, the tidal range is often less than half a metre. In contrast, in Canada's Bay of Fundy, where the shape of the bay funnels the water, the difference between high and low tide can be more than fifteen metres.","Tides have practical importance. Fishermen and sailors plan their journeys around them, and tides shape coastal habitats where many animals live. Engineers are also developing ways to produce electricity from the movement of tidal water. Unlike wind and sunlight, tides can be predicted years in advance, which makes them a potentially reliable source of renewable energy."],"q":[{"n":1,"s":"What is the passage mainly about?","o":["how to plan a holiday at the beach","the life of animals on the coast","the history of sailing","what causes tides and why they vary"],"k":3,"ty":"main idea","e":"The passage explains the causes and variations of tides.","h":"أسباب المد والجزر وتغيرها."},{"n":2,"s":"According to paragraph 2, what is the main cause of tides?","o":["the wind","the Moon's gravity","the Earth's heat","the shape of the coast"],"k":1,"ty":"detail","e":"'The main cause of tides is the gravity of the Moon.'","h":"جاذبية القمر."},{"n":3,"s":"Why does a second bulge form on the side of the Earth away from the Moon?","o":["The Sun pulls the water towards it.","The wind pushes the water there.","The Moon pulls the solid Earth more strongly than the far water.","The Earth's rotation creates waves."],"k":2,"ty":"cause–effect","e":"The water on the far side is 'left behind'.","h":"الماء البعيد يتخلف."},{"n":4,"s":"Why do tides arrive about fifty minutes later each day?","o":["The Earth is slowing down.","The Sun changes position every hour.","The Moon is moving in its orbit.","Coastlines are always changing shape."],"k":2,"ty":"cause–effect","e":"Paragraph 3 explains this.","h":"حركة القمر في مداره."},{"n":5,"s":"The word 'combine' in paragraph 4 is closest in meaning to","o":["work together","cancel each other","disappear","change direction"],"k":0,"ty":"vocabulary in context","e":"The forces work together to produce bigger tides.","h":"combine تعني تتحد."},{"n":6,"s":"What does the writer say about the name 'spring tides'?","o":["It means the tides happen only in spring.","It is not related to the season of spring.","It refers to fresh water springs.","It was given by sailors in Canada."],"k":1,"ty":"detail","e":"'The name has nothing to do with the season'.","h":"لا علاقة له بالربيع."},{"n":7,"s":"When do neap tides occur?","o":["at every full moon","when the Sun and Moon pull at right angles","when the Sun, Moon and Earth are in a line","only in enclosed seas"],"k":1,"ty":"detail","e":"Paragraph 4 explains neap tides.","h":"عندما تتعامد القوتان."},{"n":8,"s":"Why are the tides in the Bay of Fundy so large?","o":["The Moon is closer to Canada.","The bay is in an enclosed sea.","Strong winds blow there all year.","The shape of the bay funnels the water."],"k":3,"ty":"cause–effect","e":"Paragraph 5 gives the reason.","h":"شكل الخليج."},{"n":9,"s":"Which statement best paraphrases the last sentence of the passage?","o":["Tides are more powerful than wind and sunlight.","Because tides are predictable, they could provide dependable clean energy.","Tidal energy is already the world's main energy source.","Tides change so much that they cannot be used for energy."],"k":1,"ty":"paraphrase","e":"Predictable → reliable source of renewable energy.","h":"قابلة للتنبؤ فهي مصدر موثوق."},{"n":10,"s":"How is the passage mainly organized?","o":["It tells the story of one scientist.","It explains causes, then variations, then practical uses.","It compares tides in two countries only.","It lists arguments for and against tidal energy."],"k":1,"ty":"organization","e":"Causes (2–3) → variations (4–5) → uses (6).","h":"أسباب ثم تغيرات ثم استخدامات."}]},{"t":"The ancient city of Petra","p":["Hidden among the rugged mountains of southern Jordan lies Petra, one of the most extraordinary archaeological sites in the world. Its most famous buildings are not constructed from stone blocks but carved directly into the pink and red sandstone cliffs, which is why it is often called the 'Rose City'. In 1985, Petra was declared a UNESCO World Heritage Site, and in 2007 it was named one of the New Seven Wonders of the World.","Petra was the capital of the Nabataeans, an Arab people who controlled the trade routes of northern Arabia more than two thousand years ago. Caravans carrying incense, spices, silk and other valuable goods passed through their territory on the way from southern Arabia and India to Egypt, Syria and the Mediterranean. The Nabataeans grew wealthy by protecting these caravans, providing them with water and charging taxes on the goods.","Water was the key to Petra's success. The region receives very little rain, yet the city may have supported a population of around twenty thousand people. The Nabataeans were brilliant water engineers. They cut channels into the rock, built dams to control sudden floods and stored water in huge underground cisterns. Some of their channels carried water for many kilometres from springs outside the city. This system allowed them to grow gardens and even to build a large swimming pool and garden complex in the centre of the city.","Visitors usually enter Petra through the Siq, a narrow gorge about one kilometre long, with rock walls up to eighty metres high. At the end of the Siq, the most famous monument suddenly appears: Al-Khazneh, or 'the Treasury'. Despite its name, it was probably a royal tomb. Its elegant front, about forty metres high, combines local styles with Greek and Roman decoration, showing how the Nabataeans were influenced by the cultures they traded with.","Petra began to decline after the Romans took control of the region in 106 CE and trade routes moved to the sea. Later, a series of earthquakes damaged the city, and by the Middle Ages it had been largely abandoned, known only to local Bedouin. In 1812, a Swiss traveller, Johann Ludwig Burckhardt, heard stories of a lost city and, disguised as a traveller from the region, persuaded a local guide to take him there. His reports made Petra famous in Europe.","Today, Petra receives hundreds of thousands of visitors each year, and tourism is vital for the local economy. However, this popularity brings risks. Wind, rain and salt are slowly wearing away the soft sandstone, and the large number of visitors adds to the damage. Conservation experts are working to protect the monuments while allowing people to continue to experience this remarkable place. Interestingly, the Nabataeans also built a second great city, Hegra, in what is now AlUla in Saudi Arabia, which has recently opened to visitors."],"q":[{"n":11,"s":"Why is Petra often called the 'Rose City'?","o":["because of the colour of its rock","because roses grow there","because it was built by a queen named Rose","because it smells of perfume"],"k":0,"ty":"cause–effect","e":"Buildings are carved into pink and red sandstone.","h":"لون الصخر."},{"n":12,"s":"How did the Nabataeans become wealthy?","o":["by mining gold in the mountains","by selling sandstone to Rome","by controlling and taxing trade caravans","by farming large areas of land"],"k":2,"ty":"detail","e":"Paragraph 2 explains this.","h":"التحكم في القوافل."},{"n":13,"s":"What is the main idea of paragraph 3?","o":["Petra had a very rainy climate.","Clever water management made the city possible.","The Nabataeans built a swimming pool for tourists.","Floods destroyed the city."],"k":1,"ty":"insertion / paragraph function","e":"'Water was the key to Petra's success.'","h":"إدارة المياه."},{"n":14,"s":"The word 'cisterns' in paragraph 3 refers to","o":["large containers for storing water","narrow mountain paths","royal tombs","trade caravans"],"k":0,"ty":"vocabulary in context","e":"Water was stored in underground cisterns.","h":"خزانات مياه."},{"n":15,"s":"What does the design of Al-Khazneh show about the Nabataeans?","o":["They copied Egyptian pyramids.","They disliked foreign styles.","They used it to store money.","They were influenced by the cultures they traded with."],"k":3,"ty":"inference","e":"It combines local, Greek and Roman styles.","h":"تأثرهم بالثقافات الأخرى."},{"n":16,"s":"Despite its name, what was the Treasury probably used as?","o":["a bank","a royal tomb","a market","a water tank"],"k":1,"ty":"detail","e":"'it was probably a royal tomb'.","h":"قبر ملكي."},{"n":17,"s":"Which of the following is NOT mentioned as a reason for Petra's decline?","o":["a disease that killed its people","Roman control of the region","trade moving to the sea","earthquakes"],"k":0,"ty":"NOT / EXCEPT","e":"Disease is not mentioned.","h":"المرض غير مذكور."},{"n":18,"s":"Why did Burckhardt disguise himself?","o":["to avoid Roman soldiers","to sell goods in the market","to persuade a local guide to take him to Petra","to hide from earthquakes"],"k":2,"ty":"purpose","e":"He persuaded a guide while disguised.","h":"لإقناع الدليل."},{"n":19,"s":"What is the writer's attitude towards tourism in Petra?","o":["It is important but must be managed carefully.","It should be stopped completely.","It causes no problems.","It is unimportant for the economy."],"k":0,"ty":"attitude / tone","e":"Tourism is vital, but popularity brings risks.","h":"مهمة لكن تحتاج إدارة."},{"n":20,"s":"Why does the writer mention Hegra at the end?","o":["to compare Jordan's and Saudi Arabia's economies","to explain why Petra declined","to describe a Roman city","to show another Nabataean city that can be visited today"],"k":3,"ty":"purpose","e":"The Nabataeans also built Hegra, now open to visitors.","h":"مدينة نبطية أخرى."}]},{"t":"How children acquire their first language","p":["By the age of five, most children can understand thousands of words and produce complex sentences, even though nobody has formally taught them the rules of grammar. How children achieve this so quickly is one of the most fascinating questions in the study of human development.","Language learning begins even before birth. In the last months of pregnancy, babies can hear sounds from outside the womb, and studies show that newborns prefer their mother's voice and the rhythm of the language they heard while in the womb. In their first year, babies move from crying and cooing to babbling, repeating syllables such as 'ba-ba' and 'ma-ma'. Gradually, their babbling begins to sound like the language around them.","Most children produce their first recognizable words around their first birthday. For several months, vocabulary grows slowly, but at around eighteen months, many children experience a 'vocabulary explosion', learning several new words a day. At about two, they begin combining words into short phrases, such as 'more milk' or 'daddy gone'. These early sentences leave out small words but follow a logical order.","One of the most revealing features of children's speech is their mistakes. An English-speaking child might say 'I goed to the park' or 'two mouses'. Children have never heard adults say these words, so they cannot simply be copying. Instead, the mistakes show that children have worked out general rules, such as adding '-ed' for the past tense, and are applying them too widely. Linguists call this overgeneralization, and it is seen in children learning Arabic and many other languages too.","Researchers have long debated how children manage this. The linguist Noam Chomsky argued that humans are born with an innate ability for language, a kind of universal grammar that helps children make sense of what they hear. Other researchers emphasize the role of experience. They point out that children hear millions of words in their early years and are very good at detecting patterns. Most experts today believe that both nature and nurture play important roles.","What is clear is that interaction matters. Children learn best when adults talk with them, not just to them, responding to their attempts to communicate, asking questions and reading stories together. Studies suggest that young children learn far less language from screens than from real conversations. For parents, the message is simple: talking, listening and reading to children every day can make a lasting difference."],"q":[{"n":21,"s":"What question does the passage mainly address?","o":["How do children learn their first language so quickly?","Why do children make so many mistakes?","When should children start school?","How many languages can a child learn?"],"k":0,"ty":"main idea","e":"Paragraph 1 states the central question.","h":"كيف يتعلم الأطفال لغتهم الأولى."},{"n":22,"s":"According to paragraph 2, what do newborn babies prefer?","o":["silence","music without words","the voices of other babies","their mother's voice"],"k":3,"ty":"detail","e":"'newborns prefer their mother's voice'.","h":"صوت الأم."},{"n":23,"s":"What happens at around eighteen months?","o":["Children start babbling.","Many children learn new words very quickly.","Children stop making mistakes.","Children start reading."],"k":1,"ty":"detail","e":"The 'vocabulary explosion'.","h":"انفجار المفردات."},{"n":24,"s":"The phrase 'leave out' in paragraph 3 is closest in meaning to","o":["repeat","invent","shout","omit"],"k":3,"ty":"vocabulary in context","e":"Early sentences omit small words.","h":"leave out تعني يحذف."},{"n":25,"s":"Why does the writer mention 'I goed to the park'?","o":["to show that children copy adults' mistakes","to prove that English is difficult","to describe a child's favourite place","to show that children apply grammar rules they have discovered"],"k":3,"ty":"purpose","e":"Children have worked out rules and apply them too widely.","h":"تطبيق قاعدة مكتشفة."},{"n":26,"s":"What is 'overgeneralization'?","o":["learning too many words at once","speaking more than one language","using a general rule in cases where it does not apply","copying adults exactly"],"k":2,"ty":"detail","e":"Paragraph 4 explains the term.","h":"تعميم القاعدة خطأً."},{"n":27,"s":"What did Chomsky argue?","o":["Children learn only by copying.","Screens are the best teachers.","Grammar should be taught early.","Humans are born with an ability for language."],"k":3,"ty":"detail","e":"Paragraph 5 describes his view.","h":"قدرة فطرية."},{"n":28,"s":"What is the view of most experts today, according to the passage?","o":["Only innate ability matters.","Only experience matters.","The question can never be answered.","Both nature and experience are important."],"k":3,"ty":"claim / evidence","e":"'both nature and nurture play important roles'.","h":"الفطرة والتجربة."},{"n":29,"s":"What can be inferred from the last paragraph?","o":["Real conversation is more useful than screen time for language.","Children should not watch any television.","Reading is less important than talking.","Parents should correct every mistake."],"k":0,"ty":"inference","e":"Children learn far less from screens than from real conversations.","h":"المحادثة أنفع من الشاشات."},{"n":30,"s":"Which sentence best summarizes the passage?","o":["Children learn grammar mainly from formal lessons.","Language learning begins at school age.","Children learn language through natural ability and rich interaction with others.","Children's mistakes show that they are not learning."],"k":2,"ty":"summary / conclusion","e":"It combines the main ideas of the whole passage.","h":"قدرة طبيعية وتفاعل."}]},{"t":"The economics of recycling","p":["Recycling is often presented as a simple way to protect the environment: we sort our waste, and it is turned into new products. In reality, whether recycling makes economic sense depends on a complex balance of costs, prices and markets. Understanding this balance helps explain why some materials are recycled far more than others.","Collecting and sorting waste is expensive. Trucks, workers, sorting machines and processing plants all cost money. For recycling to pay for itself, the value of the recovered material must be higher than the cost of collecting and processing it. If it is cheaper to make a product from new raw materials, companies have little reason to buy recycled ones.","Aluminium is the classic success story. Making a new can from recycled aluminium uses about ninety-five per cent less energy than producing aluminium from bauxite ore. Because energy is expensive, recycled aluminium is valuable, and aluminium cans can be recycled again and again without losing quality. As a result, in many countries, a large proportion of cans are recycled. Paper and cardboard are also widely recycled, although their fibres become shorter each time.","Plastic is a much more difficult case. There are many different types of plastic, and they usually cannot be recycled together. Plastic packaging is often dirty or mixed with other materials, which makes sorting costly. Furthermore, new plastic is made from oil, so when oil prices are low, new plastic can be cheaper than recycled plastic. For many years, wealthy countries exported large amounts of plastic waste to other countries, especially in Asia. However, after China stopped accepting most foreign plastic waste in 2018, many cities found themselves with nowhere to send it.","Governments use several tools to improve the economics of recycling. Deposit schemes add a small charge to bottles and cans, which customers get back when they return them. Some countries make producers responsible for the cost of collecting and recycling their packaging, encouraging them to design products that are easier to recycle. Others charge landfill taxes, making it more expensive to bury waste.","Economists also stress that recycling is not the first solution. The most effective strategies are to reduce waste in the first place and to reuse products where possible. Recycling remains important, but it works best as part of a wider system that values resources throughout their life. In Saudi Arabia, national targets aim to divert most waste away from landfill in the coming years, which will require both new infrastructure and changes in everyday habits."],"q":[{"n":31,"s":"What is the main argument of the passage?","o":["Recycling is always profitable.","Plastic is easier to recycle than aluminium.","The success of recycling depends on economic factors.","Governments should stop recycling programmes."],"k":2,"ty":"main idea","e":"The passage explains the balance of costs, prices and markets.","h":"النجاح يعتمد على العوامل الاقتصادية."},{"n":32,"s":"According to paragraph 2, when does recycling pay for itself?","o":["when people sort their waste carefully","when the recovered material is worth more than processing costs","when trucks are electric","when governments ban new products"],"k":1,"ty":"detail","e":"The value must be higher than the cost.","h":"عندما تفوق القيمة التكلفة."},{"n":33,"s":"Why is recycled aluminium valuable?","o":["Recycling it saves a great deal of energy.","Aluminium ore is impossible to find.","Cans are made of paper.","It is used only once."],"k":0,"ty":"cause–effect","e":"It uses about 95% less energy.","h":"يوفر الطاقة."},{"n":34,"s":"Which of the following is NOT mentioned as a difficulty with recycling plastic?","o":["There are many types of plastic.","Packaging is often dirty.","Plastic cannot be melted.","New plastic can be cheaper when oil prices are low."],"k":2,"ty":"NOT / EXCEPT","e":"Melting is not discussed as impossible.","h":"عدم الصهر غير مذكور."},{"n":35,"s":"What happened after 2018?","o":["China began buying more plastic waste.","Many cities had nowhere to send their plastic waste.","Plastic became cheaper to recycle.","Oil prices rose sharply."],"k":1,"ty":"cause–effect","e":"China stopped accepting foreign plastic waste.","h":"لم يعد للمدن مكان لإرسالها."},{"n":36,"s":"The word 'exported' in paragraph 4 is closest in meaning to","o":["burned","produced","cleaned","sent to other countries"],"k":3,"ty":"vocabulary in context","e":"Wealthy countries sent waste abroad.","h":"صدّرت."},{"n":37,"s":"How do deposit schemes encourage recycling?","o":["Customers get money back when they return bottles and cans.","Producers pay a fine for every bottle.","Waste is buried at a lower cost.","Customers pay less for new bottles."],"k":0,"ty":"detail","e":"Paragraph 5 explains this.","h":"استرداد المبلغ."},{"n":38,"s":"What is the purpose of landfill taxes?","o":["to pay recycling workers","to reduce the price of cans","to make burying waste more expensive","to build new landfills"],"k":2,"ty":"purpose","e":"Landfill taxes make it more expensive to bury waste.","h":"جعل الدفن مكلفًا."},{"n":39,"s":"According to economists, what should come before recycling?","o":["burning waste for energy","exporting waste","reducing and reusing","building more landfills"],"k":2,"ty":"detail","e":"Paragraph 6: reduce waste first and reuse.","h":"التقليل وإعادة الاستخدام."},{"n":40,"s":"How does the writer develop the discussion in paragraphs 3 and 4?","o":["by contrasting a successful material with a difficult one","by telling a personal story","by listing historical dates","by describing a recycling machine"],"k":0,"ty":"organization","e":"Aluminium (success) vs plastic (difficult).","h":"المقارنة بين مادتين."}]}],"i":"Read each passage and answer the questions that follow. Choose the best answer (A, B, C or D).","iar":"اقرأ كل نص ثم أجب عن الأسئلة التي تليه، واختر الإجابة الصحيحة."},{"id":"S","name":"Sentence Structure","ar":"تركيب الجمل","min":35,"from":41,"to":70,"g":[{"i":"Choose the word or phrase that best completes the sentence.","err":false,"q":[{"n":41,"s":"I ______ for this company since I left university.","o":["am working","work","have been working","was working"],"k":2,"ty":"sentence completion","e":"have been working — Duration up to now: present perfect continuous.","h":"المضارع التام المستمر."},{"n":42,"s":"The documents ______ to the manager by the end of the day.","o":["will be sent","will send","are sending","sent"],"k":0,"ty":"sentence completion","e":"will be sent — Future passive.","h":"المبني للمجهول."},{"n":43,"s":"Hardly anyone ______ the answer to the last question.","o":["didn't know","not knew","knew","knew not"],"k":2,"ty":"sentence completion","e":"knew — Hardly is already negative; no second negative.","h":"Hardly منفية بذاتها."},{"n":44,"s":"My sister, ______ lives in Abha, is a pharmacist.","o":["that","which","who","whom"],"k":2,"ty":"sentence completion","e":"who — Non-defining clause for a person: who (not that).","h":"who في الجملة غير المحددة."},{"n":45,"s":"If I had known about the traffic, I ______ earlier.","o":["would leave","would have left","will leave","had left"],"k":1,"ty":"sentence completion","e":"would have left — Third conditional.","h":"الشرط الثالث."},{"n":46,"s":"She suggested ______ a taxi because it was raining.","o":["to take","take","taking","took"],"k":2,"ty":"sentence completion","e":"taking — suggest + -ing.","h":"suggest + -ing."},{"n":47,"s":"We had our car ______ at the new garage.","o":["repair","repairing","to repair","repaired"],"k":3,"ty":"sentence completion","e":"repaired — Causative: have something + past participle.","h":"التركيب السببي."},{"n":48,"s":"The more you read, ______ your vocabulary becomes.","o":["richer","the richest","more rich","the richer"],"k":3,"ty":"sentence completion","e":"the richer — the more …, the + comparative.","h":"كلما … كلما."},{"n":49,"s":"He ______ have taken my umbrella by mistake. It was next to his.","o":["might","mustn't","can't to","should to"],"k":0,"ty":"sentence completion","e":"might — Past possibility: might have + past participle.","h":"احتمال في الماضي."},{"n":50,"s":"I wish I ______ more attention in class last year.","o":["paid","would pay","have paid","had paid"],"k":3,"ty":"sentence completion","e":"had paid — Regret about the past: wish + past perfect.","h":"التمني عن الماضي."},{"n":51,"s":"By next June, she ______ her degree.","o":["will have finished","will finish","finishes","has finished"],"k":0,"ty":"sentence completion","e":"will have finished — Completed before a future time: future perfect.","h":"المستقبل التام."},{"n":52,"s":"The manager asked us ______ the report before Thursday.","o":["completing","complete","to complete","that complete"],"k":2,"ty":"sentence completion","e":"to complete — ask + object + to + verb.","h":"ask + to."},{"n":53,"s":"______ the heavy rain, the match continued.","o":["Although","Despite","Because","However"],"k":1,"ty":"sentence completion","e":"Despite — Despite + noun.","h":"Despite."},{"n":54,"s":"There's ______ milk left. We need to buy some.","o":["a few","many","hardly no","hardly any"],"k":3,"ty":"sentence completion","e":"hardly any — Uncountable, almost none: hardly any.","h":"hardly any."},{"n":55,"s":"Neither the students nor the teacher ______ aware of the change.","o":["were","was","are being","have"],"k":1,"ty":"sentence completion","e":"was — With neither … nor, the verb agrees with the nearer subject.","h":"المطابقة مع الأقرب."},{"n":56,"s":"When I was a child, my grandfather ______ tell us stories every evening.","o":["was","would","use","is used to"],"k":1,"ty":"sentence completion","e":"would — would for repeated past actions.","h":"would للعادة في الماضي."},{"n":57,"s":"The new hospital, ______ cost over a billion riyals, opened last month.","o":["which","that","what","who"],"k":0,"ty":"sentence completion","e":"which — Non-defining clause for a thing: which.","h":"which."},{"n":58,"s":"Not only ______ the exam, but she also got the highest mark.","o":["she passed","did she pass","she did pass","passed she"],"k":1,"ty":"sentence completion","e":"did she pass — Not only at the start: inversion with did.","h":"القلب بعد Not only."},{"n":59,"s":"It's high time we ______ for the airport.","o":["left","leave","will leave","have left"],"k":0,"ty":"sentence completion","e":"left — It's high time + past simple.","h":"It's time + الماضي."},{"n":60,"s":"Had I known you were ill, I ______ you.","o":["would visit","visited","will visit","would have visited"],"k":3,"ty":"sentence completion","e":"would have visited — Inverted third conditional.","h":"شرط ثالث مقلوب."}]},{"i":"Choose the underlined part (A, B, C or D) that is incorrect.","err":true,"q":[{"n":61,"s":"The number of students (A) who study online (B) have (C) increased (D) dramatically.","o":["who","have","increased","dramatically"],"k":1,"ty":"error identification","e":"have — The number of … is singular: has increased.","h":"The number مفرد."},{"n":62,"s":"I (A) have been (B) living here (C) since (D) three years.","o":["have been","living","since","three years"],"k":3,"ty":"error identification","e":"three years — for + a period: for three years.","h":"for مع المدة."},{"n":63,"s":"(A) Despite of the warnings, (B) many people (C) went (D) swimming.","o":["Despite of","many","went","swimming"],"k":0,"ty":"error identification","e":"Despite of — despite takes no of.","h":"despite بلا of."},{"n":64,"s":"If she (A) had (B) studied harder, she (C) would pass the (D) exam last year.","o":["had","studied","would pass","exam"],"k":2,"ty":"error identification","e":"would pass — Third conditional: would have passed.","h":"would have passed."},{"n":65,"s":"The report, (A) that was published (B) last week, (C) contains several (D) errors.","o":["that","last","contains","errors"],"k":0,"ty":"error identification","e":"that — Non-defining clauses use which, not that.","h":"which في غير المحددة."},{"n":66,"s":"Ali (A) avoided (B) answering the (C) question because he (D) didn't knew the answer.","o":["avoided","answering","question","didn't knew"],"k":3,"ty":"error identification","e":"didn't knew — didn't + base verb: didn't know.","h":"didn't مع المصدر."},{"n":67,"s":"She (A) must (B) have (C) forget her keys, because she (D) couldn't open the door.","o":["must","have","forget","couldn't"],"k":2,"ty":"error identification","e":"forget — must have + past participle: forgotten.","h":"التصريف الثالث."},{"n":68,"s":"The (A) advice you gave me (B) were (C) very (D) useful.","o":["advice","were","very","useful"],"k":1,"ty":"error identification","e":"were — advice is uncountable and singular: was.","h":"advice مفرد."},{"n":69,"s":"I wish I (A) could (B) speak Chinese (C) as fluently (D) like my brother.","o":["could","speak","as","like"],"k":3,"ty":"error identification","e":"like — as … as for equal comparison.","h":"as … as."},{"n":70,"s":"By the time we (A) have arrived, the guests (B) had already (C) left (D) the party.","o":["have arrived","had","left","the"],"k":0,"ty":"error identification","e":"have arrived — Past time clause: By the time we arrived.","h":"الماضي: arrived."}]}],"iar":"الأسئلة من ٤١ إلى ٦٠: اختر الكلمة أو العبارة التي تكمل الجملة إكمالًا صحيحًا."},{"id":"L","name":"Listening Comprehension","ar":"فهم المسموع","min":30,"from":71,"to":90,"g":[{"rec":1,"a":"M11-L-01","q":[{"n":71,"s":"When will the interview take place?","o":["tomorrow at ten","on Sunday at ten","on Monday afternoon","on Sunday at two o'clock"],"k":3,"ty":"correction","e":"Sunday morning is difficult; they agree on two o'clock on Sunday.","h":"الأحد الساعة الثانية."}],"t":"Rescheduling a job interview","sc":["Situation: A woman receives a phone call from a company. (75 words)","Man: Good morning, Ms. Al-Shehri. This is Fahad from Delta Engineering. I'm calling about your interview tomorrow at ten.","Woman: Yes, I'm looking forward to it.","Man: Unfortunately, the manager has to travel unexpectedly. Would it be possible to move the interview to Sunday at the same time?","Woman: Sunday morning is difficult for me, I'm afraid. I have a university exam. Could we make it Sunday afternoon instead?","Man: Certainly. Shall we say two o'clock?","Woman: That's perfect. Thank you."]},{"rec":2,"a":"M11-L-02","q":[{"n":72,"s":"How does the hotel solve the problem?","o":["by sending him to another hotel","by giving the guest a better room at no extra cost","by giving him a discount on dinner","by asking the other guest to leave"],"k":1,"ty":"detail","e":"They offer a suite at no extra cost with breakfast.","h":"غرفة أفضل دون تكلفة."}],"t":"A double booking at a hotel","sc":["Situation: A guest is at a hotel reception desk. (78 words)","Man: Good evening. I have a reservation for two nights under the name Al-Qahtani.","Woman: Let me see. Oh, I'm very sorry, sir. It seems the room was booked twice by mistake, and the other guest has already checked in.","Man: That's very inconvenient. I've been travelling all day.","Woman: I completely understand. We'd like to offer you a suite on the top floor at no extra cost, and breakfast will be included for both nights.","Man: Well, that's very generous. Thank you."]},{"rec":3,"a":"M11-L-03","q":[{"n":73,"s":"Why do the customers want to change tables?","o":["It is too noisy where they are sitting.","It is too cold near the window.","They want to sit with their family.","Their table is dirty."],"k":0,"ty":"reason","e":"They are next to the speakers and can hardly hear each other.","h":"المكان صاخب."}],"t":"Asking for a quieter table","sc":["Situation: A couple are speaking to a waiter in a restaurant. (62 words)","Woman: Excuse me, would it be possible to move to another table? We're right next to the speakers, and we can hardly hear each other.","Man: Of course. There's a table by the window in the family section, which is much quieter. It'll be ready in about five minutes.","Woman: That's fine. We don't mind waiting.","Man: Would you like to order drinks while you wait?"]},{"rec":4,"a":"M11-L-04","q":[{"n":74,"s":"What caused the mistake on the report?","o":["The digits were typed in the wrong order.","The student's test was lost.","The teacher marked the wrong test.","The office used last year's grades."],"k":0,"ty":"reason","e":"'The numbers were typed the wrong way round.'","h":"الأرقام كُتبت معكوسة."}],"t":"A wrong grade on a report","sc":["Situation: A student is speaking to her teacher. (63 words)","Woman: Excuse me, Ms. Huda. I think there's a mistake on my report. It says I got sixty-eight in chemistry, but my test was eighty-six.","Woman: Let me check my records. You're right. The numbers were typed the wrong way round.","Woman: Will it be corrected before the reports go to parents?","Woman: Yes, I'll inform the office today, and they'll print a new report for you."]},{"rec":5,"a":"M11-L-05","q":[{"n":75,"s":"What will the first man probably do?","o":["wait for the IT department","copy his slides and use his colleague's laptop","cancel his presentation","buy a new cable"],"k":1,"ty":"inference","e":"'Use my laptop.' — 'Good idea.'","h":"يستخدم حاسوب زميله."}],"t":"Borrowing a projector cable","sc":["Situation: Two colleagues are preparing for a presentation. (48 words)","Man: My laptop doesn't connect to this projector. It needs a different cable.","Man: I think the IT department has one, but they're closed until one o'clock.","Man: My presentation starts at twelve!","Man: Don't worry. Use my laptop. Just copy your slides onto a memory stick.","Man: Good idea. That's much quicker."]},{"rec":6,"a":"M11-L-06","q":[{"n":76,"s":"What does the man suggest?","o":["calling a repair company themselves","moving to another building","helping Umm Saleh move","writing a letter signed by all the residents"],"k":3,"ty":"function","e":"'Let's write a letter together and ask all the residents to sign it.'","h":"خطاب يوقعه السكان."}],"t":"A broken lift in an apartment block","sc":["Situation: Two neighbours meet on the stairs of their building. (66 words)","Woman: The lift is out of order again. That's the third time this month.","Man: I know. I complained to the building manager last week, but nothing happened.","Woman: It's really difficult for Umm Saleh on the eighth floor. She can't climb all these stairs.","Man: You're right. Let's write a letter together and ask all the residents to sign it. Then the owner will have to take it seriously."]},{"rec":7,"a":"M11-L-07","q":[{"n":77,"s":"When can the woman use the gym on Saturdays?","o":["in the morning","all day","in the evening","not at all"],"k":2,"ty":"detail","e":"On Saturdays, it's from four to ten in the evening.","h":"مساءً."}],"t":"Asking about a gym's ladies' hours","sc":["Situation: A woman is calling a sports centre. (59 words)","Woman: Hello. Could you tell me when the gym is open for ladies?","Man: Ladies' hours are from eight in the morning until two in the afternoon, Sunday to Thursday. On Saturdays, it's from four to ten in the evening.","Woman: So there are no evening sessions during the week?","Man: Not at the moment, but we're planning to add some next month."]},{"rec":8,"a":"M11-L-08","q":[{"n":78,"s":"What probably happened to the parcel?","o":["The driver delivered it to the wrong apartment.","The neighbour's wife opened it.","It was stolen from the door.","It was never sent. Longer conversations"],"k":0,"ty":"inference","e":"'the driver must have mixed up the numbers'.","h":"سُلِّم للشقة الخطأ."}],"t":"A parcel left at the wrong door","sc":["Situation: A man knocks on his neighbour's door. (68 words)","Man: Sorry to bother you. I'm expecting a parcel, and the delivery app says it was left at the door, but it's not there.","Man: Oh, there was a box outside my door this morning. I thought it was for my wife. Let me check the name.","Man: It should say Majed Al-Harbi, apartment twelve.","Man: Yes, here it is. Apartment twelve. I'm sorry, the driver must have mixed up the numbers."]},{"rec":9,"a":"M11-L-09","q":[{"n":79,"s":"What topic does the professor suggest?","o":["the history of the botanical garden","how animals survive in the desert","comparing how two desert plants store water","the effects of rain on crops"],"k":2,"ty":"detail","e":"He suggests comparing two desert plants.","h":"مقارنة نباتين صحراويين."},{"n":80,"s":"Why won't the student need to travel to the desert?","o":["The project is only based on reading.","She can study desert plants in the university garden.","The professor will bring samples.","Desert plants grow everywhere in the city."],"k":1,"ty":"reason","e":"'The university's botanical garden has several desert species'.","h":"حديقة الجامعة."}],"t":"Choosing a research topic in biology","sc":["Situation: A student is talking to her biology professor. (158 words)","Woman: Dr. Kamal, I need to choose a topic for my research project, and I'm not sure where to start.","Man: What areas of biology interest you most?","Woman: I'm interested in plants, especially how they survive in dry conditions.","Man: That's a good area for Saudi Arabia. You could compare how two desert plants store water.","Woman: That sounds interesting, but wouldn't I need to travel to the desert?","Man: Not necessarily. The university's botanical garden has several desert species, and you could do most of the work there.","Woman: That would be much easier. How long should the project be?","Man: About five thousand words. And make sure you read at least ten recent articles before you plan your experiment.","Woman: I'll start with the library database this week. Could I send you a short plan next Monday so you can check that I'm going in the right direction?","Man: Of course. Send it by email, and we'll discuss it in my office hours on Tuesday."]},{"rec":10,"a":"M11-L-10","q":[{"n":81,"s":"Why will every dish need a label?","o":["The principal wants to know the prices.","Parents want the recipes.","Some students have allergies.","The labels will be part of a competition."],"k":2,"ty":"reason","e":"'Some students have allergies, so every dish will need a label'.","h":"بسبب الحساسية."},{"n":82,"s":"Why will the final show probably be held in the courtyard?","o":["The hall may be too small for everyone.","The hall is being repaired.","Students prefer to be outside.","The courtyard has better lighting."],"k":0,"ty":"inference","e":"The hall holds only three hundred people.","h":"القاعة صغيرة."}],"t":"Planning a cultural week at school","sc":["Situation: Two teachers are planning a school event. (158 words)","Man: The principal wants us to organize a cultural week next term. Any ideas?","Man: Our school has students from more than fifteen countries. Each class could represent one country.","Man: Good idea. They could prepare posters, traditional food and a short presentation.","Man: We should be careful with the food, though. Some students have allergies, so every dish will need a label listing its ingredients.","Man: Absolutely. And what about the final day?","Man: We could have a cultural show in the hall, with songs, poems and traditional clothes, and invite parents.","Man: The hall holds only three hundred people. With parents, that might not be enough.","Man: Then let's hold the show outside in the courtyard in the evening, when it's cooler.","Man: Perfect. I'll write a proposal for the principal by Thursday, including a budget for decorations and a timetable for each day. Can you ask the class teachers which countries they would like to represent?","Man: Sure. I'll send them a message this afternoon."]},{"rec":11,"a":"M11-L-11","q":[{"n":83,"s":"Why does the second woman think a hotel hall might not be suitable?","o":["It would be too noisy.","The cost could be too high for some classmates.","It is too far away.","It does not have a garden."],"k":1,"ty":"reason","e":"'many of our classmates are students or have young families, so the cost matters'.","h":"التكلفة."},{"n":84,"s":"What will the second woman do tonight?","o":["check the rest house","book a hotel hall","create a group on social media","prepare the decorations Talks and lectures"],"k":2,"ty":"detail","e":"'I'll create a group on social media tonight.'","h":"إنشاء مجموعة."}],"t":"Deciding where to hold a reunion","sc":["Situation: Two former classmates are planning a reunion. (162 words)","Woman: It's been ten years since we graduated from high school. We really should organize a reunion.","Woman: I agree. Where should we hold it? A restaurant might be too noisy for talking.","Woman: What about renting a hall in a hotel? It's more expensive, but we'd have privacy.","Woman: True, but many of our classmates are students or have young families, so the cost matters.","Woman: Then how about my family's rest house? It has a large garden and a big sitting room, and it's free.","Woman: That's a wonderful idea! We could each bring a dish and share the cost of decorations.","Woman: Exactly. I'll check which weekends it's available, and you can start contacting everyone.","Woman: I'll create a group on social media tonight. I still have most people's numbers, and the others can be added by their friends. Let's also invite our old teachers. I'm sure some of them would love to come.","Woman: What a lovely idea. Ms. Latifa would be so happy to see us."]},{"rec":12,"a":"M11-L-12","q":[{"n":85,"s":"What is the main purpose of the lecture?","o":["to describe the history of Rome","to teach students how to drive trucks","to explain how different bridge designs handle forces","to compare the cost of building materials"],"k":2,"ty":"purpose","e":"The lecturer explains forces and three bridge types.","h":"شرح تصاميم الجسور والقوى."},{"n":86,"s":"Why are some Roman stone arches still standing?","o":["They were rebuilt recently.","Stone is very strong in compression.","They carry very little weight.","They are made of steel."],"k":1,"ty":"reason","e":"'Stone is very strong in compression'.","h":"الحجر قوي في الضغط."},{"n":87,"s":"Which statement about suspension bridges is correct?","o":["They are only used for short distances.","They are the cheapest type of bridge.","Their weight is carried only by stone arches.","Their cables work in tension."],"k":3,"ty":"detail","e":"'Here, the cables are in tension.'","h":"الكابلات في الشد."}],"t":"Lecture: how bridges carry weight","sc":["Situation: An engineering lecturer is speaking to first-year students. (236 words)","Lecturer: Good morning. Today we'll look at a simple but important question: how do bridges carry weight? Every bridge must deal with two main forces. The first is compression, a pushing force that squeezes material together. The second is tension, a pulling force that stretches material apart. A good bridge design spreads these forces so that no single part has to carry too much. Let's consider three common types. The simplest is the beam bridge, which is basically a horizontal beam supported at each end. When a heavy truck crosses, the top of the beam is compressed while the bottom is stretched. Beam bridges are cheap, but they are only practical for short distances. The second type is the arch bridge. The curved shape of the arch turns the weight into compression and pushes it outwards and down into the supports at each end. Stone is very strong in compression, which is why some Roman stone arches are still standing after two thousand years. The third type is the suspension bridge, used for the longest spans. The road hangs from vertical cables attached to huge main cables, which pass over tall towers and are anchored firmly in the ground. Here, the cables are in tension. Modern steel cables are extremely strong in tension, allowing spans of more than two kilometres. Next week, we'll test model bridges in the laboratory to see which design carries the most weight."]},{"rec":13,"a":"M11-L-13","q":[{"n":88,"s":"Why was the water tower built?","o":["to provide a place for tourists to visit","to produce electricity","to collect rainwater","to store water and keep a steady pressure as the city grew"],"k":3,"ty":"purpose","e":"The growing city needed storage and steady pressure.","h":"التخزين والضغط."},{"n":89,"s":"Why is water usually pumped into the tank at night?","o":["Demand for water is lower then.","It is cooler at night.","Electricity is free at night.","The pipes are cleaned during the day."],"k":0,"ty":"reason","e":"'usually at night when demand is lower'.","h":"الطلب أقل ليلًا."},{"n":90,"s":"What is the main role of the tower today?","o":["the city's only water supply","a desalination plant","an office building","a symbol of the city's modernization"],"k":3,"ty":"detail","e":"It is preserved as a symbol.","h":"رمز لتحديث المدينة."}],"t":"Talk: the history of the Riyadh water tower","sc":["Situation: A guide is speaking to visitors at a landmark in Riyadh. (230 words)","Lecturer: Welcome, everyone. The tall tower you see in front of you is the Riyadh Water Tower, one of the city's best-known landmarks. It was completed in the early 1970s, at a time when Riyadh was growing very rapidly. As the population increased, the city needed a reliable way to store water and keep a steady pressure in the pipes, so that water could reach homes even on upper floors. Water towers do this using gravity. Water is pumped up into the large tank at the top, usually at night when demand is lower. During the day, when people need more water, it flows down through the pipes under its own weight, without needing extra pumps. The tower is about sixty metres high, and its design was inspired by the shape of a tall glass, making it both practical and elegant. Today, Riyadh's water system relies on much larger modern networks, including desalinated water piped hundreds of kilometres from the coast, so the tower is no longer essential for water supply. However, it has been preserved as a symbol of the city's modernization. The surrounding area has been turned into a park, and in the evening the tower is lit up in different colours. For many residents who grew up in the city, it brings back memories of family outings and a Riyadh that was much smaller than it is today."]}],"i":"You will hear 13 recordings: 8 short conversations (one question each), 3 longer conversations (two questions each) and 2 talks (three questions each). Read the questions before each recording, then choose the best answer.","iar":"ستسمع ثلاثة عشر تسجيلًا: ثماني محادثات قصيرة (سؤال لكل منها)، وثلاث محادثات أطول (سؤالان لكل منها)، وحديثين أو محاضرتين (ثلاثة أسئلة لكل منهما). اقرأ الأسئلة قبل بدء كل تسجيل."},{"id":"C","name":"Composition Analysis","ar":"التحليل الإنشائي","min":20,"from":91,"to":100,"g":[{"q":[{"n":91,"s":"Which sentence is the best topic sentence for the paragraph?","o":["Glaciers are found in high mountains.","Climate change is already affecting many parts of the world.","Some regions receive a lot of rain.","Scientists use computers to study the weather."],"x":["______ Rising temperatures are melting glaciers, and sea levels are slowly rising. In some regions, droughts are becoming longer, while in others, heavy storms are more frequent."],"k":1,"ty":"topic sentence / thesis","e":"The details describe current effects of climate change.","h":"آثار تغير المناخ."},{"n":92,"s":"Which sentence best fills the blank in the paragraph?","o":["Libraries usually have group study rooms.","Explaining ideas to others helps them understand the material more deeply.","Some students live far from the university.","Social events are important for students."],"x":["Many students prefer studying in groups. ______ However, group study can also become a social event where little work is done."],"k":1,"ty":"complete the paragraph","e":"A benefit before 'However' introduces a drawback.","h":"فائدة قبل However."},{"n":93,"s":"The government has (A) introduced new rules (B) which (C) aims to reduce (D) traffic accidents.","o":["introduced","which","aims","traffic"],"k":2,"ty":"error","e":"which refers to rules (plural): aim.","h":"rules جمع: aim."},{"n":94,"s":"Which sentence does NOT belong in the paragraph?","o":["Sentence 1","Sentence 2","Sentence 3","Sentence 4"],"x":["(1) Remote work has changed the way many companies operate. (2) Employees save time because they do not commute. (3) Companies can reduce the cost of renting offices. (4) Traffic in large cities is often heavy in the morning. (5) However, managers sometimes find it harder to build team spirit."],"k":3,"ty":"irrelevant sentence","e":"The traffic sentence is general and does not develop the point about how companies operate.","h":"جملة المرور عامة."},{"n":95,"s":"Which sentence is the best topic sentence for the paragraph?","o":["Many villages are far from cities.","Video calls require a good internet connection.","Telemedicine is making health care more accessible.","Doctors study for many years."],"x":["______ It allows doctors to talk to patients through video calls, send prescriptions online and monitor patients' health from a distance. This is especially useful for people living in remote villages."],"k":2,"ty":"topic sentence / thesis","e":"The details describe telemedicine and its benefits.","h":"الطب عن بعد."},{"n":96,"s":"Choose the best order for the sentences.","o":["2 – 4 – 3 – 1","3 – 2 – 4 – 1","2 – 3 – 1 – 4","2 – 3 – 4 – 1"],"x":["(1) As a result, the number of visitors has increased dramatically.","(2) In recent years, Saudi Arabia has invested heavily in tourism.","(3) New visas have made it easier for foreigners to visit.","(4) In addition, historical sites such as AlUla have been opened to the public."],"k":3,"ty":"best order","e":"topic → visas → In addition → As a result.","h":"تسلسل منطقي."},{"n":97,"s":"Which sentence best fills the blank in the paragraph?","o":["Plastic bags are cheap to produce.","They often end up in the sea, where they harm turtles and other marine animals.","Some shops use paper bags.","Turtles live for many years."],"x":["Plastic bags take hundreds of years to break down. ______ As a result, several countries have banned them or introduced a small charge for each bag."],"k":1,"ty":"complete the paragraph","e":"The harm leads to 'As a result' (bans).","h":"الضرر يؤدي إلى المنع."},{"n":98,"s":"Which sentence is the best concluding sentence for the paragraph?","o":["For these reasons, music education deserves a place in every school.","Pianos are very expensive.","Some instruments are difficult to carry.","Many famous musicians started young."],"x":["Learning a musical instrument requires patience and discipline. It improves concentration and memory, and it gives people a way to express their feelings. Studies also show that it can reduce stress. ______"],"k":0,"ty":"concluding sentence","e":"A conclusion drawn from the benefits.","h":"خلاصة من الفوائد."},{"n":99,"s":"If the company (A) had invested in new technology, it (B) would not (C) lose so many (D) customers last year.","o":["had invested","would not","lose","customers"],"k":2,"ty":"error","e":"Third conditional: would not have lost.","h":"would not have lost."},{"n":100,"s":"Which word or phrase best fills the blank?","o":["Moreover","Nevertheless","Otherwise","In contrast Teacher Section — Mock 11"],"x":["The new metro will reduce traffic in Riyadh. ______, it will lower air pollution, since fewer people will drive."],"k":0,"ty":"transition / connector","e":"Moreover adds a second benefit.","h":"إضافة."}]}],"i":"Read each paragraph or set of sentences and choose the best answer (A, B, C or D).","iar":"اقرأ كل فقرة أو مجموعة جمل واختر الإجابة الصحيحة."}]};
